FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://petiht.com/freelanceragent

# Konbit Work Events API
Send proof of work (a merged pull request, a client's approval email, a finished
calendar session, an Upwork or Notion update) to your Konbit workspace. Claude
reviews it, matches it to an open milestone and proposes a PayPal payout. The
server then applies your signed mandate: the payout is sent at once, waits for
your approval, or is blocked.

Evidence is treated as untrusted text. It can never add a payee or raise a limit.

Use the generated SDKs from Zapier steps, GitHub Actions or your own scripts.


## Authentication
This API uses Custom Header for its authentication.

The parameters that are needed to be sent for this type of authentication are as follows:
+ `X-Konbit-Key` - Workspace key from Mandate → Work-event webhook. It is shown once when created.

# Group Work events

Send work evidence to the payout agent and read its decision.

## HookPhp [/hook.php]

### submitWorkEvent [POST]
Stores the evidence, asks the Konbit agent (Claude) to review it, and returns the
review together with any payout plans it created. A plan's `decision` tells you
what the signed mandate allowed: `auto` (paid with PayPal Payouts), `ask`
(waiting for the freelancer's approval) or `block` (refused by policy).

+ Request (application/json)

    + Attributes (WorkEventInput)


    + Body

            {
                "source": "github",
                "title": "Pull request #42 merged",
                "text": "PR #42 \"Landing page\" was merged and deployed. Client: Landing page is live and looks great, thank you Jean!"
            }


+ Response 201 (application/json)

        The agent reviewed the evidence.

    + Attributes (WorkEventResult)


    + Body

            {"event_id":12,"status":"done","risk":"low","summary":"PR #42 was merged and the client confirmed the landing page is live. I proposed Jean's $250.00 milestone.","plans":[{"plan_id":7,"title":"Jean Pierre · Landing page live","total_cents":25000,"decision":"ask","status":"needs_approval"}]}


+ Response 400 (application/json)

        The body is not valid JSON.

    + Attributes (ApiError)


    + Body

            {"error":"invalid_json"}


+ Response 401 (application/json)

        Missing or wrong X-Konbit-Key.

    + Attributes (ApiError)


    + Body

            {"error":"unauthorized","message":"Send your workspace key in the X-Konbit-Key header."}


+ Response 413 (application/json)

        The body is larger than 50 KB.

    + Attributes (ApiError)


    + Body

            {"error":"too_large"}


+ Response 422 (application/json)

        The evidence was rejected (for example, too short) or could not be reviewed.

    + Attributes (ApiError)


    + Body

            {"error":"rejected","message":"The evidence text is too short."}


+ Response 429 (application/json)

        Rate limited (20 events per hour per workspace).

    + Attributes (ApiError)


    + Body

            {"error":"rate_limited","message":"Up to 20 events per hour."}



## HookPhp [/hook.php{?event_id}]

### getWorkEvent [GET]
Returns the agent's review of an event submitted earlier, with the current status of every payout plan it created.
+ Parameters
    + event_id (number, required)

        The `event_id` returned by submitWorkEvent.

        + Sample: 12

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The event and its plans.

    + Attributes (WorkEventResult)


    + Body

            {"event_id":12,"status":"done","risk":"low","summary":"PR #42 was merged and the client confirmed the landing page is live.","plans":[{"plan_id":7,"title":"Jean Pierre · Landing page live","total_cents":25000,"decision":"ask","status":"sent"}]}


+ Response 401 (application/json)

        Missing or wrong X-Konbit-Key.

    + Attributes (ApiError)


    + Body

            {"error":"unauthorized","message":"Send your workspace key in the X-Konbit-Key header."}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such event in this workspace.

    + Attributes (ApiError)


    + Body

            {"error":"not_found"}




# Data Structures

## WorkEventInput (object)
Work evidence to send to the agent.

### Properties
+ `source` (enum[string], optional) - Where the evidence came from.
    + `email`
    + `github`
    + `calendar`
    + `upwork`
    + `notion`
    + `slack`
    + `api`
    + `manual`
+ `title`: `Pull request #42 merged` (string, optional) - A short title, such as an email subject.
+ `text`: `PR #42 "Landing page" was merged and deployed.` (string, required) - The raw evidence. It is treated as untrusted data.


## WorkEventResult (object)
The agent's review of one piece of evidence.

### Properties
+ `event_id`: `12` (number, required) - Event identifier.
+ `status` (enum[string], required) - Review result: done = payout proposed, ignored = no action, flagged = suspicious.
    + `new`
    + `analyzing`
    + `done`
    + `ignored`
    + `flagged`
    + `error`
+ `risk` (enum[string], optional) - How risky the agent and the risk scan judged the evidence.
    + `low`
    + `medium`
    + `high`
+ `summary`: `PR #42 was merged and the client confirmed the landing page is live.` (string, optional, nullable) - The agent's one or two sentence summary.
+ `plans` (array[PayoutPlan], optional) - Payout plans created from this evidence.


## PayoutPlan (object)
A proposed or completed PayPal payout.

### Properties
+ `plan_id`: `7` (number, required) - Plan identifier.
+ `title`: `Jean Pierre · Landing page live` (string, required) - Who is paid and for what.
+ `total_cents`: `25000` (number, required) - Total in US cents.
+ `decision` (enum[string], required) - What the signed mandate decided for a payout plan.
    + `auto`
    + `ask`
    + `block`
+ `status` (enum[string], required) - The payout plan's current status.
    + `needs_approval`
    + `blocked`
    + `scheduled`
    + `sending`
    + `sent`
    + `paid`
    + `partial`
    + `failed`
    + `rejected`


## ApiError (object)
An error response.

### Properties
+ `error`: `unauthorized` (string, required) - A short machine-readable error code.
+ `message`: `Send your workspace key in the X-Konbit-Key header.` (string, optional) - A human-readable explanation, when available.

